## Summary

Wired the **`Border.glow : Int -> Color -> Attribute msg`** kernel, mirroring the landed `Border.shadow` template but as a curried **arity-2** kernel (no record), across all layers:

| Layer | Site |
|---|---|
| `sky_kernels/lib.rs` | `BorderGlow` variant + `d("Border","glow",2,Ui,"ui_border_glow_")` decl + `ALL` + `is_ui` match |
| `sky_types/constrain.rs` | `stdlib_scheme` arm `fun(int(), fun(color(), attr(var(0))))` + `FIRST_SCHEMED` membership (keeps `migrated_set_burndown` exact) |
| `sky_lower/lower.rs` | `callee_arity` `Ok(2)` group (next to `Ui.paddingXY`) + dispatch `("Border","glow")` |
| `sky_ir/pretty.rs` | `"Border.glow"` |
| `sky_backend_rust/naming.rs` | `"ui_border_glow_"` |
| `sky_backend_rust/emit_expr.rs` | 2-positional-arg emit arm (blur + colour, no record destructure) |
| `runtime/helpers.rs` | `ui_border_glow_<M>(blur, c)` → `AttrStyle("box-shadow", "0px 0px {blur}px 0px {colour}")`, colour via the same `color_to_css` boundary |
| `runtime/render.rs` | **test-first** regression `border_glow_renders_box_shadow` (verified the value clears the `SafeCssValue` gate so it isn't silently dropped) |

`glow` was already a registered Std.Ui.Border qualifier in `canon/env.rs` with no kernel backing — a pure wiring gap. No suppression, no hacks; every compiler-enforced exhaustive `KernelFn` match is covered. Per orchestrated-lane instructions I did **not** run the full workspace gate (the orchestrator integrates + gates all lanes on the shared target); the sibling `innerShadow` lane shares these registry files and will exercise the reconcile path.

